#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:1
msgid "Serving a Nix store via SSH"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:3
msgid ""
"You can tell Nix to automatically fetch needed binaries from a remote Nix "
"store via SSH. For example, the following installs Firefox, automatically "
"fetching any store paths in Firefox’s closure if they are available on the "
"server `avalon`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:8
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-env --install --attr nixpkgs.firefox --substituters ssh://"
"alice@avalon\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:12
msgid ""
"This works similar to the binary cache substituter that Nix usually uses, "
"only using SSH instead of HTTP: if a store path `P` is needed, Nix will "
"first check if it’s available in the Nix store on `avalon`. If not, it will "
"fall back to using the binary cache substituter, and then to building from "
"source."
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:18
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:20
msgid ""
"The SSH substituter currently does not allow you to enter an SSH passphrase "
"interactively. Therefore, you should use `ssh-add` to load the decrypted "
"private key into `ssh-agent`."
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:24
msgid ""
"You can also copy the closure of some store path, without installing it into "
"your profile, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:27
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-store --realise /nix/store/m85bxg…-firefox-34.0.5 --substituters\n"
"ssh://alice@avalon\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:32
msgid "This is essentially equivalent to doing"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:39
msgid ""
"You can use SSH’s _forced command_ feature to set up a restricted user "
"account for SSH substituter access, allowing read-only access to the local "
"Nix store, but nothing more. For example, add the following lines to "
"`sshd_config` to restrict the user `nix-ssh`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:53
msgid ""
"On NixOS, you can accomplish the same by adding the following to your "
"`configuration.nix`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:56
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"nix.sshServe.enable = true;\n"
"nix.sshServe.keys = [ \"ssh-dss AAAAB3NzaC1k... bob@example.org\" ];\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:61
msgid ""
"where the latter line lists the public keys of users that are allowed to "
"connect."
msgstr ""
